XB-Kidux-Name-en: Tux Typing
XB-Kidux-Description-en: An arcade typing tutor starring Tux the penguin: practise keyboard speed and accuracy by typing falling letters and words, in the child's language.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: Tux Typing
XB-Kidux-Description-es: Juego arcade de mecanografía con el pingüino Tux: practica la velocidad y la precisión en el teclado escribiendo las letras y palabras que caen, en el idioma del niño.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 6-12
XB-Kidux-Before: gcompris
Description: Kidux learning module: Tux Typing, a typing course for ages six to twelve
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is Tux Typing: letters and words fall from the sky, and a child
 catches them by typing them, one level harder each time, with the words
 and the menus in the child's language where Tux Typing has them.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
